{"advice_coverage":{"additional_concern_fix_plans":0,"additional_concerns":0,"finding_assessment_slots":0,"finding_assessments":0,"finding_fix_plans":0,"interpretation":"Fix plans are proposals, not executed patches or validated safeguards. Finding/check assessment counts include actual model answers only; synthesized omitted slots are separate. Missing model advice remains absent; static guidance stays available.","model_check_assessments":2,"model_check_fix_plans":2,"omitted_finding_assessments":0,"static_findings":0,"static_fix_plans":0},"analyst":{"advisory_only":true,"check_status_counts":{"insufficient_evidence":1,"potential_gap":1},"control_assessments":[{"check_assessments":[{"analysis":{"boundary":"The visible boundary is caller-controlled user_url entering tool_forward, crossing the admission predicate, and becoming the destination of a server-side HTTP POST. Actual agent or MCP registration is not supplied.","conclusion_limits":"Only the local flow is established. No code was executed, and deployed reachability, library behavior, DNS handling, network isolation, and external egress policy remain unresolved.","counterevidence":"The rejection branch is present, but its predicate does not restrict lane 1. The sibling caller uses a constant destination on lane 0, and redirects are disabled. The excerpts describe an inert fixture. These alternatives limit the claim but do not establish destination restrictions for lane 1.","risk_hypothesis":"A caller could select an internal or metadata destination and reach requests.post because lane 1 makes _admit true regardless of the URL."},"check":"Restrict destinations and schemes at connection time; revalidate DNS resolution and each redirect.","check_index":1,"citations":[{"end_line":7,"evidence_id":"src-ea8f5ad7a1e9b55c0a223d85","path":"agent.py","quote":"return dispatch(1, user_url, user_content)","source_sha256":"3f8ad0be3946f65cce7217f596f63de4fa2bde0cd62d8f397702d7bd83c1c199","start_line":7},{"end_line":18,"evidence_id":"src-c76b9846c312b1d8e2392d1c","path":"delivery.py","quote":"def _admit(a, b):\n    return a == 1 or b == \"https://approved.invalid\"","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":17},{"end_line":41,"evidence_id":"src-6a02164f7498f198ded37c26","path":"delivery.py","quote":"def dispatch(lane, addr, record):\n    if not _admit(lane, addr):\n        raise ValueError(\"Unsupported destination\")\n    return requests.post(addr, json={\"record\": record}, timeout=5,\n                         allow_redirects=False)","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":37}],"model_supplied":true,"reason":"The visible caller-selected URL enters dispatch with lane 1. The admission predicate accepts that lane independently of the destination, allowing the URL to reach requests.post without a visible destination or scheme restriction in this flow. Redirects are explicitly disabled, which limits redirect-based exposure. The constant destination used by the sibling lane does not constrain lane 1. Connection-time address restrictions and DNS enforcement are not established by the supplied evidence. This is an unverified concern in a declared inert fixture, not evidence of deployed exploitability.","recommended_actions":{"agent_mcp_relevance":"If exposed as an agent or MCP tool, caller-controlled user_url crosses into server-side outbound HTTP, potentially using network access unavailable to the caller.","applicability":"Apply changes to any operational implementation represented by this fixture. Deployment reachability and existing transport or egress controls require owner confirmation.","steps":["Replace the unconditional lane-1 admission with a destination policy applied to every caller-controlled URL; explicitly allow required schemes and approved destinations.","Enforce resolved-address restrictions at connection time through a controlled transport or egress proxy, covering loopback, private, link-local, metadata, and IPv6 destinations without a validation-to-connection DNS race.","Retain allow_redirects=False. If redirects become necessary, validate every target and its connection destination before following it."],"verification":["Review that every relevant lane invokes the same destination policy and cannot bypass it through lane selection.","Use isolated transport observations to verify blocked addresses receive no connections, including after DNS changes.","Retain regression coverage showing redirect responses are not followed."]},"status":"potential_gap","verification_steps":["Have the owner establish whether this fixture represents a reachable agent or MCP tool and identify caller authorization and external egress restrictions.","Review the deployed transport and destination policy for allowed schemes, resolved IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, and enforcement against the actual connection destination.","In an authorized isolated environment, verify that disallowed destinations cannot receive a connection and that redirect responses are never followed."]},{"analysis":{"boundary":"Required coverage spans caller-provided URLs, admission decisions, DNS resolution, actual outbound connections, and redirect handling.","conclusion_limits":"No test suite, case matrix, or runtime results were supplied. Test absence and operational applicability cannot be inferred, and runtime validation remains outstanding.","counterevidence":"The visible request disables redirects, reducing one relevant exposure. The fixture declaration was considered as a possible nonoperational context. Neither establishes test coverage; tests outside the submitted excerpts remain possible.","risk_hypothesis":"Incomplete destination testing could leave lane-dependent admission bypasses or address-interpretation differences undetected."},"check":"Test loopback, private/link-local IPv4 and IPv6, cloud metadata, alternate encodings, and redirect-to-private cases.","check_index":2,"citations":[{"end_line":1,"evidence_id":"src-1c85609fb313cbfd95eb25cd","path":"delivery.py","quote":"\"\"\"Inert review fixture: network calls below must never be executed.\"\"\"","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":1},{"end_line":41,"evidence_id":"src-6a02164f7498f198ded37c26","path":"delivery.py","quote":"return requests.post(addr, json={\"record\": record}, timeout=5,\n                         allow_redirects=False)","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":40}],"model_supplied":true,"reason":"The supplied excerpts contain no test cases or results covering loopback, private/link-local IPv4 and IPv6, cloud metadata, alternate encodings, or redirects to private destinations. Disabling redirects is relevant implementation evidence but does not establish that these cases were tested. The declared fixture context further limits conclusions about operational coverage; omitted tests may exist.","recommended_actions":{"agent_mcp_relevance":"Destination tests should exercise the caller-controlled tool boundary through to the outbound transport, since predicate-only tests cannot establish which destination actually receives a connection.","applicability":"First identify the operational implementation and existing tests. Do not execute the submitted inert fixture or contact real metadata or internal services.","steps":["Obtain existing test artifacts before concluding that coverage is missing.","Where coverage is missing, add isolated cases for loopback, private and link-local IPv4 and IPv6, metadata destinations, alternate address encodings, and redirects to prohibited destinations.","Include controlled DNS changes and assert the observed connection destination; cover lane 1 and the fixed-destination sibling to detect lane-dependent bypasses."],"verification":["Have an owner review the case matrix against every address category in this acceptance check.","Retain isolated test results demonstrating rejection before prohibited connections and no follow-up connection after a redirect response."]},"status":"insufficient_evidence","verification_steps":["Request the relevant test inventory and results covering every required address class, alternate encodings, and redirects to private destinations.","Have the owner validate the operational implementation in an authorized isolated harness with controlled DNS and connection observations, including both visible caller lanes."]}],"control_id":"EXEC-05","provenance":{"assurance":"Code support is not a control pass or proof of deployed behavior.","citation_validation":"Exact quote in submitted excerpt; semantic interpretation remains advisory.","evidence_selection_boundary":"Validated file-ID/line requests within captured manifest snapshots only.","model_selected_evidence":true,"model_selected_evidence_allowed":true,"model_tools_enabled":false,"runtime_execution":false,"static_results_modified":false},"review_status":"reviewed","static_status":"no_pattern_detected","title":"Prevent SSRF and unsafe network destinations","validation":"hybrid","validation_established":false}],"coverage":{"attempted_controls":1,"batch_size":1,"call_budget":3,"calls_made":2,"catalog_checks":2,"catalog_controls":1,"disabled_checks":0,"disabled_controls":0,"evidence":{"budget_exhausted":[],"bytes_charged":1243,"bytes_read":1243,"candidate_rankings_dropped":0,"candidate_snippets":3,"characters_selected":1147,"controls_total":1,"controls_with_evidence":1,"controls_without_evidence":[],"evidence_files":2,"failed_read_bytes_charged":0,"file_read_attempts":2,"files_read":2,"files_verified":2,"full_repository_review":false,"limitations":["Keyword-selected excerpts are partial context and do not prove implementation, absence, effectiveness, or compliance.","Only unchanged manifest files are eligible; scanner exclusions and unsupported files remain outside this review.","Credentials and environment files are excluded; other redaction is best-effort and source can contain sensitive data.","Read budgets reserve one sentinel byte and conservatively charge failed read attempts, even if failure happened before any source bytes were read.","No target code is executed, imported, installed, or contacted; repository instructions cannot change retrieval.","Runtime behavior and missing evidence require additional validation; an empty control mapping is not a pass."],"limits":{"max_bytes":2000000,"max_candidates_per_control":64,"max_chars":60000,"max_chars_per_excerpt":2000,"max_excerpts_per_control":4,"max_file_bytes":1000000,"max_files":200,"max_lines_per_excerpt":12,"max_snippets":240},"manifest_files":2,"requested_characters_selected":92,"scope":"bounded_excerpts_from_unchanged_scanner_manifest_files","selection_method":"deterministic_control_keywords_and_findings","skipped_counts":{},"skipped_files":[],"snippets_selected":3},"excluded_checks":0,"excluded_controls":0,"justified_checks":0,"justified_controls":0,"omitted_checks":0,"reviewed_controls":1,"time_budget_seconds":900.0,"total_checks":2,"total_controls":1,"unreviewed_control_ids":[],"validated_controls":0},"enabled":true,"errors":[],"evidence":[{"end_line":12,"end_line_complete":true,"evidence_id":"src-ea8f5ad7a1e9b55c0a223d85","kind":"source_excerpt","path":"agent.py","source_sha256":"3f8ad0be3946f65cce7217f596f63de4fa2bde0cd62d8f397702d7bd83c1c199","start_line":1,"text":"\"\"\"Inert author-created review fixture. Do not import or execute this module.\"\"\"\nfrom delivery import dispatch\n\n\ndef tool_forward(user_url, user_content):\n    \"\"\"Forward a caller-selected record through the delivery boundary.\"\"\"\n    return dispatch(1, user_url, user_content)\n\n\ndef fixed_forward(record):\n    \"\"\"A sibling entry point uses a constant destination and different lane.\"\"\"\n    return dispatch(0, \"https://approved.invalid\", record)"},{"end_line":12,"end_line_complete":true,"evidence_id":"src-1c85609fb313cbfd95eb25cd","kind":"source_excerpt","path":"delivery.py","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":1,"text":"\"\"\"Inert review fixture: network calls below must never be executed.\"\"\"\nimport requests\n\n\n# The dispatcher accepts two lanes. A reviewer needs the predicate body and\n# each caller's lane selection before deciding what the condition establishes.\n# Definition hints make the predicate discoverable even when keyword-selected\n# seed excerpts do not retain it. These gaps intentionally separate the three\n# relevant regions for a bounded-context investigation demonstration.\n\n\n"},{"end_line":41,"end_line_complete":true,"evidence_id":"src-6a02164f7498f198ded37c26","kind":"source_excerpt","path":"delivery.py","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":37,"text":"def dispatch(lane, addr, record):\n    if not _admit(lane, addr):\n        raise ValueError(\"Unsupported destination\")\n    return requests.post(addr, json={\"record\": record}, timeout=5,\n                         allow_redirects=False)"},{"end_line":36,"end_line_complete":true,"evidence_id":"src-c76b9846c312b1d8e2392d1c","kind":"source_excerpt","path":"delivery.py","source_sha256":"b7995f3334ed328ff74ebdf4834b75fe7b4a84cb608c6e8408490f89b1cd8c9c","start_line":13,"text":"\n\n\n\ndef _admit(a, b):\n    return a == 1 or b == \"https://approved.invalid\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"}],"investigation":{"conclusion_calls":1,"enabled":true,"excerpt_character_budget":120000,"excerpt_characters_used":1239,"inventory_characters":491,"limits":{"max_chars_per_request":4000,"max_inventory_chars":32000,"max_inventory_files":200,"max_lines_per_request":80,"max_requests_per_round":8,"max_requests_total":128,"max_symbols_per_file":12},"max_rounds_per_batch":2,"protocol":"manifest_snapshot_ranges_v1","receipts":[{"check_id":"EXEC-05:1","check_index":1,"control_id":"EXEC-05","counterevidence":"Seek effecti